{
  "case_id": "2011-11-161",
  "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 11-161, Armour v. City of Indianapolis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark T. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STANCIL: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The city chose a method for abandoning its sewer funding mechanism that left Petitioners paying 30 times more than their next-door neighbors to connect to their neighborhood sewer project simply because Petitioners had paid their tax bills in full."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I thought there were a lot more than -- there are 20 different lots, 20 different -- there are -- I mean, when -- what's your view of -- of how the cutoff should work? Do they have to refund all the money, everybody who, in fact, ever paid a Barrett Law assessment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Why can the State, when they have, let's say, 10,000 people who have already paid their assessments -- well, why doesn't it have to give them back their money, on your theory? That's my simple question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Have we ever decided an equal protection case on the basis that the -- the State who had violated the -- the Constitution can't afford to pay for it? Is there any case that supports that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I'm saying is when they want to change tax policy, having already said these taxpayers are the same and entitled under law to equal treatment, they can't just say, well, it would be too expensive on us to treat them equally"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stancil",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They could have increased those monthly fees under STEP, the new program. I mean, that's how they paid for the rest of these projects. They're paying off the bonds of the old projects by charging everybody in Indianapolis $10 more a month."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So, you really are saying that amnesty programs are out of the question if the risk is imposed equally on everyone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you tell me -- I'm curious to know, if other States have provisions like the Barrett Law and they're concerned about this, can they provide in the initial documents a -- a promise that there will be no forgiveness, so that there would be a contract clause sort of argument against what happened here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the law that created the violation is Resolution 101, than the remedy in every other area of constitutional law, including sex discrimination, is clearly that the State has the option. They can level up or they can level down."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, the question, I would have thought, in our Court is whether that's a rational distinction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would look to Carmichael v. Southern Coal where, you know, this Court is confronting a case where the State says, you know, we're not going to tax employers -- employers who are smaller than eight, because, you know, the game is not worth the candle."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We've got an estimate from our controller that's going to cost us $200,000 to upgrade and maintain this system. We really don't want to spend that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What did the Court mean when they said, ordinarily, extension is the proper course?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: It involves -- you know, I don't -- I know the number of projects. It's like 20 projects. So, I'm guessing it's at least 1,000 people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: When you say \"the other case,\" you mean every other project? Because that's -- that's, what, a class action; right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: No, actually it would -- plus this one. So, it would be a little over 3."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: What do you do with the hypothetical about the income tax and the sales tax?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is there some identified or identifiable demographic difference between the two groups that either justifies or could on -- on a remand justify the different treatment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: The question, I guess, is, is that rational?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86b656dc615aac74da0faa136a14c0e218406a2f321378fe8411eee3a141690d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86b656dc615a-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
